Why this project is AGPL-3.0-only
  The wire envelope (24-byte little-endian header, kinds, flags, touch and key
  payload layout), the AVCC/avcC frame model, the JSON control message set and
  the projection session rules were worked out by reading the OpenXPlay project's
  published source (OpenXPlay-Stream, OpenXPlay-Relay, both AGPL-3.0-only, and
  OpenXPlay-WinUI). Deriving this prototype from that material puts it under the
  same license, and because the receiver is reached over a network, section 13
  applies: anyone who interacts with a running copy over a network must be able
  to get its source. Serve it with a link to this repository, or ship the source
  alongside the pages.

What is NOT in here
  No code from OpenXPlay, DiPlay, xcertplay, or any commercial CarPlay box was
  copied into this repository: the protocol shapes were reimplemented in
  JavaScript from observations of the published format.
  No Apple protocol is implemented. There is no iAP2, no AirPlay pairing, no
  CarPlay control session, no RTSP media set, and no MFi authentication, and no
  Apple certificate, private key or other accessory identity is bundled, derived
  or emulated. CarPlay is a trademark of Apple Inc.; this is an independent
  prototype with no affiliation with or endorsement by Apple.

Trademark note
  "OpenXPlay" is the name of the project whose architecture this imitates, used
  here only to describe what this prototype is modelled on.

Device-iOS fixtures
  device-ios/Fixtures/* are generated by scripts/ios-fixtures.mjs: a 720p H.264 encode produced by
  ffmpeg's libx264, and envelopes/records written by src/protocol and src/media. They are data
  distributed with this program under the same AGPL-3.0-only terms; libx264's own copyright and
  licence stay with FFmpeg, and nothing here links against it — it is a child process fed a pipe.

Swift sources
  device-ios/Sources and device-ios/App carry the same AGPL-3.0-only header as the rest of the
  project. The wire format and session rules they implement were likewise worked out from
  OpenXPlay-Stream's published material; no OpenXPlay code was copied into them.
